From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rvwasm <rvwasm@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:41:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] wasm: copy_thread: no mm for a kernel thread, and the
 child's fields

For every kernel thread p->mm is NULL, and copy_thread() read binfmt through
it, from the first bytes of memory (Wasm has no null page fault; every stray
NULL write of any program on the machine lands there too). When that word
was 0 it then wrote zeroes through current->mm, NULL again for kthreadd.
The fields meant are the child's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/wasm/kernel/process.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
index 7cfbbd7..d50fc8b 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
@@ -236,13 +236,14 @@ int copy_thread(struct task_struct *p, const struct kernel_clone_args *args)
 			child_switch_stack->tls = args->tls;
 	}
 
-	if (!p->mm->binfmt) {
+	/* (A kernel thread has no mm; the fields are the child's, not ours.) */
+	if (p->mm && !p->mm->binfmt) {
 		/* These are normally not zeroed out in copy_process(). */
-		current->mm->start_code = 0;
-		current->mm->end_code = 0;
-		current->mm->start_stack = 0;
-		current->mm->start_data = 0;
-		current->mm->end_data = 0;
+		p->mm->start_code = 0;
+		p->mm->end_code = 0;
+		p->mm->start_stack = 0;
+		p->mm->start_data = 0;
+		p->mm->end_data = 0;
 	}
 
 	return user_task_set_affinity(p);
